{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G]Way back yonder a  [C]long time [G]ago
[G]Daddy worked a man called  [D]Cotton-Eyed  [G]Joe
[G]Blew into town on a  [C]travelin' [G]show
[G]Nobody danced like the  [D]Cotton-Eyed  [G]Joe
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[G]If it hadn't been for [C]Cotton-Eye [G]Joe
[G]I'd been married a [D]long time [G]ago
[G]Where did you come from, [C]where did you [G]go?
[G]Where did you come from, [D]Cotton-Eye [G]Joe?
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[G]He came to town like a [C]midwinter [G]storm
[G]He rode through the fields, so [D]handsome and [G]strong
[G]His eyes was his tools and his [C]smile was his [G]gun
[G]But all he had come for was [D]having some [G]fun
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[G]If it hadn't been for [C]Cotton-Eye [G]Joe
